 "about_text": "Parrasch heijnen is a gallery in the Boyle Heights neighborhood of Los Angeles. Its program brings together postwar Los Angeles Light and Space and geometric abstraction, work by artists associated with the historic Brockman Gallery and the Black Arts Council, and a roster of contemporary painters and sculptors working in abstraction and assemblage. The gallery represents several artist estates, including those of Peter Alexander, Tony DeLap, Forrest Bess, Marcia Hafif and Alonzo Davis, alongside living artists such as Anne Appleby, Edith Baumann, Alteronce Gumby, Xylor Jane, Kristy Luck, Mildred Howard and Christine Howard Sandoval. The gallery participates regularly in international art fairs, including Frieze, Art Basel Miami Beach, NADA, Independent and the Dallas Art/Invitational fairs, and has organized historical group presentations such as 'Brockman Days' surveying the artists of the pioneering Black-owned Brockman Gallery.",
 "source_kind": "official",
